==English==

===Etymology===
{{suffix|en|jog|er}}. The ethnic slur is a reference to [[w:Killing of Ahmaud Arbery|Ahmaud Arbery]], an African-American man who was murdered by three white assailants while jogging in 2020. There are however attestations that predate the incident. It has been used as a replacement or a [[dog whistle]] for [[nigger]] due to the fact that Apple devices used to auto-correct [[nigger]] to [[jogger]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/ˈdʒɒ.ɡə(ɹ)/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/ˈdʒɑːɡɚ/}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɒɡə(r)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A person who [[jog]]s (as exercise).
# A [[tracksuit]], particularly the [[trousers]].
# A [[printing press]] operator who removes, jogs, and stacks the [[sheet]]s or [[signature]]s of paper.
# {{lb|en|chiefly derogatory|internet slang|4chan slang}} A [[black]] person.
#: {{synonyms|en|nigger}}

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|tracksuit}}, {{l|en|joggers}}

